; SPDX-License-Identifier: 0BSD
; The recalculation floors' memory and load fixture (KERNEL.49, its first slice): Alonzo's Life on the size
; ladder's sixteenth rung, a board of 1280 by 800, 1,019,844 formula cells of one shape, as the machine loads
; it. The pass's output of Alonzo's cartridges/life/life.source.vla at 640c0a3 (0BSD there and here) with the
; ladder's definition of board-size at 1280 by 800 (engine/src/ladder.rs), its manifest left out, and the rows
; of the engine's own sheets it reads written last, as Alonzo's Cartridge::load writes them, the frame 1 and
; the seed 1 of its manifest. Its first frame is the soup, the cartridge's, sheet for sheet.
(sheet "Screen" visible)
(sheet "Palette" visible)
(cell "Palette" "A1" 0)
(cell "Palette" "B1" "#000000")
(cell "Palette" "C1" "dead")
(cell "Palette" "A2" 1)
(cell "Palette" "B2" "#FFFFFF")
(cell "Palette" "C2" "alive")
(cell "Palette" "A3" 2)
(cell "Palette" "B3" "#0000AA")
(cell "Palette" "C3" "blue")
(cell "Palette" "A4" 3)
(cell "Palette" "B4" "#00AA00")
(cell "Palette" "C4" "green")
(cell "Palette" "A5" 4)
(cell "Palette" "B5" "#00AAAA")
